; multitrack.moritz - a multitrack session (session.score) played by a score box: the same playback as the arranger's.
; Each track is a channel: its clips, its patches (an insert, an instrument, patch clips), its strip (fader, pan, mute,
; solo: the mixer's), its sends to buses (here echo, with its insert patch), then the master. Long files are read from
; disk while they play; tracks run on several cores when there are enough of them.
; Try: 1. play; 2. File > Open Session... and choose session.score: the arranger (a browser of files on the left, the
; timeline, the drawer below with the mixer); play there too, move a fader (heard as it moves: no plan is made again),
; mute the drums, solo the synth; 3. the drawer's Track tab with the echo bus current (click its name): its insert,
; edited while it plays; 4. arm a track (R), choose its input, Record: the take goes into session_media/ next to the
; session and becomes a clip, moved by the device's latency so that it lines up; 5. Render > Stereo Mix and Stems.
(patch
  (obj title comment "a multitrack session: tracks, buses, inserts, an instrument, a patch clip, strip lanes" (pos 20 12))
  (obj sub comment "play; File > Open Session... session.score: the arranger, its mixer in the drawer" (pos 20 34))
  (obj play message play (pos 20 70))
  (obj stop message stop (pos 65 70))
  (obj loc message "locate 1" (pos 110 70))
  (obj l5 message "locate 5" (pos 180 70))
  (obj tr transport 100 4 4 (pos 250 70))
  (obj sc score session session.score 2 @size 640 240 @view timeline (pos 20 105))
  (obj c1 comment "the score's own file: the arranger edits the same session (save it there, read it again here)" (pos 20 352))
  (obj rd message read (pos 20 380))
  (obj inf message info (pos 70 380))
  (obj pr print session (pos 120 410))
  (obj out dac~ (pos 20 450))
  (connect play 0 tr 0)
  (connect stop 0 tr 0)
  (connect loc 0 tr 0)
  (connect l5 0 tr 0)
  (connect rd 0 sc 0)
  (connect inf 0 sc 0)
  (connect sc 4 pr 0)
  (connect sc 0 out 0)
  (connect sc 1 out 1))
